### Sign-in, sessions and the users routes. Run the requests top to bottom.
### The API sets three cookies (op_access, op_refresh, op_csrf). REST Client
### keeps them for you, but it does not copy op_csrf into a header: the
### @csrf variable below does, once you paste the cookie's value into it.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in
@demoPassword = orderpilot-demo-password

### What the sign-in page offers. Public. With DEMO_MODE=false, demoRoles is empty.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/options

### Demo sign-in as one of the nine roles. Only with DEMO_MODE=true: otherwise this
### route does not exist and answers 404. Roles: SYSTEM_ADMIN, PRODUCT_MANAGER,
### APPROVER, SUPPORT, WAREHOUSE, FINANCE, LOGISTICS, MANAGEMENT, AUDITOR.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SYSTEM_ADMIN" }

### Sign in with the seeded email and the DEMO_PASSWORD from your .env.
### An unknown email and a wrong password get the same answer (INVALID_CREDENTIALS).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "system.admin@example.test", "password": "{{demoPassword}}" }

### Validation: a bad email is refused with VALIDATION_FAILED and a field list.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "x" }

### Who am I, what may I do, and when does the access token end.
### Without a session: 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

### Exchange the refresh cookie for a new pair. Each refresh token works once:
### sending an old one again revokes the whole sign-in (REFRESH_REUSED).
### Needs the CSRF header; without it: 403 CSRF_INVALID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Sign out. Needs the CSRF header too.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Users. Reading needs users.read, changing needs users.manage (SYSTEM_ADMIN
### holds both). Another role gets 403 FORBIDDEN, and the refusal is audited.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=1&pageSize=25

### One user. Replace the id with one from the list.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### Disable a user (never deleted). Their sessions end at their next request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/disable
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Enable them again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/enable
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
